From 605117900acc9542ac177380bde139dca197740c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Gr=C3=A9goire=20Layet?= <gregoire.layet@9elements.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 14:33:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hwmontempsensor: add support for internal NTC thermistor
 sensors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add support for non-i2c, internal NTC thermistor temperature sensors.
Use ThermistorAdcChannel as the hwmon locator.

The NTC thermistors use the driver "ntc-thermistor". This is used to
find the possible hwmon devices. The driver handles the conversion from
the measured voltage to milli-Celsius. It identifies hwmon devices
bound to that driver, reads the ADC channel from the device's DT
'io-channels' property, and matches it against the
'ThermistorAdcChannel' property of the entity-manager config.

This can be used on standalone BMC card with NTC sensors.
For example, the ASUS IPMI Expansion Card feature three headers for
NTC sensors.

The added type is not in sensorTypes as it doesn't follow existing I2C
sensors conventions. The implementation is intentionally specific to the
"ntc-thermistor" kernel driver rather than a generic platform-sensor
mechanism. A future non-i2c hwmon temp type would need its own locator
anyway, so no generic dispatch is introduced.

buildSensorConfigMaps is split into collectHwmonNames, addI2cConfig and
addThermistorConfig helpers. I2C classification behavior is
unchanged.

Tested:
Sensor value read correctly.
'''
$ busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.HwmonTempSensor \
    /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/temperature/Header2_Temp \
    xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value Value
d 24.922
'''

Property changes are propagated without restart:
'''
$ busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.HwmonTempSensor \
    /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/temperature/Header0_Temp \
    xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Threshold.Critical CriticalHigh
d 90

$ busctl set-property xyz.openbmc_project.EntityManager \
    /xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/chassis/ASUS_Kommando_IPMI_Card/Header0_Temp \
    xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.NTCThermistor.Thresholds0 Value d 98

$ busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.HwmonTempSensor \
    /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/temperature/Header0_Temp \
    xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Threshold.Critical CriticalHigh
d 98
'''

I2C Sensor value read correctly (match old behavior).
Tested on HPE ProLiant DL365 Gen11.
'''
$ busctl get-property xyz.openbmc_project.HwmonTempSensor \
  /xyz/openbmc_project/sensors/temperature/CPU_1 \
  xyz.openbmc_project.Sensor.Value Value
d 45.5
'''

